_ownerId = ownerId;
}
// rest of the code skipped
}
Our entity has no check for the ownerId, since, by receiving the argument of type UserId,
we guarantee that the value is valid. Of course, we do not check here if the supplied GUID
points to a valid user, but this was not our intention, at least for now.
However, we still have one more check for the argument validity in the entity constructor.
Let's make the entity id type a value object too by adding a ClassifiedAdId class with
the following code:
