There are a couple of new things going on here, listed as follows:
We give the value object a dependency on the currency lookup domain service.
Since we are using the interface, our domain model still has no external
dependencies.
Since we are not using the null reference to indicate that there is no currency
found for the specified code, we do not use null checks. Instead, we check if the
returned currency is valid or not. Since the CurrencyDetails.NotFound
constant has its InUse property set to false, we will throw an exception just as
we would do for any currency that exists, but is not in use.
We do not use two as the maximum number of decimal places. Instead, we get
this number from the currency lookup, so our value object becomes more
