Events change state
If we move on to the idea of Event Sourcing, events represent the fact of state change. It
means that an entity state cannot be changed without some interaction with a domain
event. However, in our code so far, the fact of changing the system state and raising a
domain event is completely separated. Let's see how we can change it.
First, we need to make some changes in the Entity base class:
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Linq;
namespace Marketplace.Framework
{
public abstract class Entity
{
private readonly List<object> _events;
protected Entity() => _events = new List<object>();
protected void Apply(object @event)
{
When(@event);
EnsureValidState();
_events.Add(@event);
}
