We have renamed the Raise method to Apply since it will not only add events to the list of
changes but physically apply the content of each event to the entity state. We do it by using
the When method, which each entity needs to implement. The Apply method also calls the
EnsureValidState method, which we previously had in the entity, but not in the base
class. By doing this, we remove the need to call this method for each operation on the
entity.
